---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Heatmap from '../../components/Heatmap.astro';
import weighting from '../../data/weighting.json';
import { allPapers } from '../../lib/data';
const areas = Object.entries(weighting.areas).map(([k, v]) => [k, `${k} ${v}`]);
const series = [...new Set(allPapers.filter((p) => p.kind === 'exam').map((p) => p.series))].reverse();
const marks = (s, area) => allPapers.filter((p) => p.series === s).reduce((n, p) => n + (weighting.byPaper[p.id]?.[area] || 0), 0);
---
<Base title="What comes up in AQA A-level Environmental Science: marks by topic, 2020–2025" description="Marks by section of the AQA Environmental Science (7447) specification for every public series, from our tagging of every question part." context="analysis">
  <h1>What comes up, paper by paper</h1>
  <p>Marks assessed under each section of the specification across the two papers in each series, from our tagging of every question part. Darker cells carry more marks; the right-hand column is the total. A part that assesses two sections counts its marks under both, and both essays of each question 11 are counted, so a column adds up to more than the 240 marks on the papers.</p>
  <Heatmap areas={areas} series={series} value={marks} title="Marks by section by series" short={(s) => s.replace('June ', 'Jun ').replace('November ', 'Nov ').replace(' 20', ' ')} />
  <p class="muted">June 2025 is the most recent series AQA has published. AQA keeps each summer's papers for teachers only for about a year, so the data here runs to the latest public series. November 2020 and November 2021 were the autumn series sat in place of the cancelled summer exams. The June 2019 papers are not on AQA's public site.</p>
  <p><a href="/what-came-up/">What came up in the latest papers</a> · <a href="/timeline/">Every paper as a timeline</a></p>
</Base>
